From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:58:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reason: JStudio cutscene payloads read big-endian

A .stb's structure (header, blocks, sequence words, paragraph headers and
the embedded function values) is converted on load by the platform
(tww_endian_stb); what its object paragraphs carry is known only to the
code reading it, so that stays big-endian and is read with
JGadget::binary::beLoad: the value iterators (TParseValue_raw_) and the
direct reads in JStudio's objects and adaptors (sound, message, actor,
camera, particle, the reserved flag/wait/jump paragraphs, variable
values). Unconverted, the title's opening cutscene (Demo51 title.stb)
did not run and the title fell back to normal play under the logo.
---
 include/JSystem/JGadget/binary.h                | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 src/JSystem/JStudio/JStudio/jstudio-object.cpp  |  7 ++++---
 src/JSystem/JStudio/JStudio/stb.cpp             |  7 ++++---
 .../JStudio/JStudio_JAudio/object-sound.cpp     |  5 +++--
 .../JStudio/JStudio_JMessage/object-message.cpp |  3 ++-
 .../JStudio_JParticle/object-particle.cpp       |  5 +++--
 .../JStudio/JStudio_JStage/object-actor.cpp     | 15 ++++++++-------
 .../JStudio/JStudio_JStage/object-camera.cpp    |  5 +++--
 src/JSystem/JStudio/JStudio_JStage/object.cpp   |  5 +++--
 9 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/JSystem/JGadget/binary.h b/include/JSystem/JGadget/binary.h
index 77339720..655527d7 100644
--- a/include/JSystem/JGadget/binary.h
+++ b/include/JSystem/JGadget/binary.h
@@ -61,10 +61,25 @@ struct TParse_header_block {
     }
 };
 
+// tww-vita: data parsed through these (JStudio cutscene payloads, JMessage)
+// stays big-endian on PC; beLoad reads a value of it (identity on the GameCube).
+template <typename T>
+inline T beLoad(const void* data) {
+#ifdef TARGET_PC
+    union { T v; u8 b[sizeof(T)]; } u;
+    const u8* s = (const u8*)data;
+    for (u32 i = 0; i < sizeof(T); i++)
+        u.b[i] = s[sizeof(T) - 1 - i];
+    return u.v;
+#else
+    return *(const T*)data;
+#endif
+}
+
 template <typename T>
 struct TParseValue_raw_ {
     typedef T ParseType;
-    static T parse(const void* data) { return (T)*(T*)data; }
+    static T parse(const void* data) { return beLoad<T>(data); }
 };
 
 template <typename T>
